# Snails - Native iOS/Android RAG App
# ====================================

# Source data (private: real names and chat history — never commit)
PS Processed/
Whatsapp PS Exports/
WhatsApp PS Exports/
# Signup sheets: names, email addresses and phone numbers for ~150 people.
PS People/

# Exports and sheets dropped loose in the repo root.
#
# The rules above cover the DIRECTORIES the pipeline reads. Nothing covered a
# file dropped at the top level on its way there, and on 2026-08-20 a
# with-media WhatsApp export sat in the root at 1.26 GB, untracked and
# unignored -- one `git add -A` from doing again what made this repository
# unpushable for seven months.
#
# Matched by shape rather than by name, because the next export will be called
# something else. A media export is 2,000 photos and 240 videos around a
# single 1.8 MB _chat.txt; strip the media before putting it in
# "Whatsapp PS Exports/", which is where the pipeline actually reads from.
#
# The .docx and screenshots rules are the same idea one step further along:
# they are SOURCES whose products are already committed and much smaller.
# "Build (2026).docx" is 29 MB and became Lucy/build-2026.md plus 6.1 MB of
# figures; screenshots/ is 10 MB of phone PNGs that became site/screens/ at a
# fifth the size. Committing both originals adds 39 MB that nothing reads, to
# the repository whose whole scar is being too big to push. Convert with
# scripts/docx_to_markdown.py and site/make_screens.sh; keep the originals
# wherever you keep the rest of the camp's paperwork.
/*.zip
/WhatsApp Chat*
/PS *.csv
/PS *.md
/Production Budget*.csv
/*.xlsx
/*.docx
/screenshots/
# "Playa data/" is the same again: three saved webapps plus two API fetches,
# 5 MB, converted to Lucy/playa-*.json by scripts/playa_data.py. The API
# files (api-art-*.json) are re-fetchable from playamap.org while it is up;
# the saved pages are not re-savable after the burn, so back the folder up
# with the corpus rather than deleting it.
/Playa data/

# Corpus and artifact backups taken before a destructive rebuild. Same size
# class as the databases themselves, and scripts/output/ is already ignored --
# these catch copies taken anywhere else.
*.pre-reingest-*
*.pre-2026-*
ps_knowledge.db.bak

# Generated databases and downloaded models
scripts/output/
scripts/models/

# RunAnywhere SDK (large binary package - clone separately)

# Swift Package Manager
.build/
.swiftpm/
Package.resolved

